Package: CONPS.JCPOS
Type: Compendium
Title: Native Plant Germination and Survival Study for Jefferson County
    Parks & Open Space
Version: 0.2.0
Date: 2026-09-22
Authors@R: c(
    person("Maggie", "Gaddis", email = "ExecutiveDirector@CoNPS.org",
           role = c("aut", "dtc"),
           comment = "Principal investigator, Colorado Native Plant Society"),
    person("Mark C.", "Otto", email = "mark.ot2o@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = "Statistical analysis"))
Description: Data, R code, and documentation for the Colorado Native Plant
    Society (CoNPS) study funded by a 2025 Jefferson County Parks & Open Space
    (JCPOS) research grant. Four forb and four grass species native to JCPOS
    properties were germinated in peat and mineral/compost media, then
    planted on North Table Mountain Park in three soil types, with and
    without fertilization, on three dates in 2025. Binomial generalized
    linear models estimate germination by species and soil type, and field
    survival by species, soil type, planting date, and fertilization.
    Run R/Germination.R and R/Survival.R from the project root; figures are
    written to doc/images/ and estimate tables to doc/tables/.
